CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=club_acronym:HEALTHPROMOTION
CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=event_type:Training/Workshop
CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=event_tags:Wellness
DTSTART:20260708T133000Z
DTEND:20260708T200000Z
UID:102a87279a278990de41948eaedd59ec5182026_1:33:09_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Mental Health First Aid Training
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2330189
DESCRIPTION:Interpreters have been requested. This training is not available to individuals outside of the RIT community.\n\nMental Health First Aid (MHFA) is a skills-based training course for anyone who wants to make their community more compassionate, informed, and prepared to support student mental health. \n\nThrough this training, you will learn:\n\nHow to describe and talk about mental health, openly and non-judgmentally.\nApproach, reassure, and support a fellow RIT community member when they are struggling with their mental health.\nExploration of what self-care looks like for you and practical applications of self-care.\nIf you have any questions, or you need clarification on anything, please do not hesitate to email Beau Gibbs at bmghcw@rit.edu.  \n\nYou will need to complete 2.5 hours of pre-work BEFORE attending the training. This pre-work will be made available to you approximately 1 week before the start of the training.\n\nThank you for your commitment to making RIT a more mentally well campus.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2330189
END:VEVENT
