CONTACT:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/FSP/rsvp_boot?id=2332433#event_host
CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=club_acronym:FSP
CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=event_type:Event
DTSTART:20260905T123000Z
DTEND:20260905T200000Z
UID:e386f5fdee2754ba2acd0bf625e58a048192026_2:43:01_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:FSP at Honoring Haudenosaunee Relationships Day @ Seneca Park Zoo
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2332433
DESCRIPTION:Join the Future Stewards Program at the Seneca Park Zoo on Saturday, September 5, 2026 for the first-ever Honoring Haudenosaunee Relationships Day.\n\nFSP will cover zoo admission for participating students. Transportation arrangements will be communicated separately based on interest and availability.\n\nThis special event was created and is being led by Kanyʌhtowa·nʌ Cheyenne Reuben-Thomas, a Seneca Park Zoo Naturalist and Indigenous ecologist who is a member of the Oneida Nation and the Tonawanda Seneca Nation.\n\nThroughout the day, the Zoo will offer educational programs centered on Haudenosaunee cultural knowledge, relationships with more-than-human relatives, and Indigenous approaches to conservation and environmental stewardship. Programs will connect ancient and modern stories with present-day conservation efforts and encourage guests to think more deeply about local species, habitats, sustainability, and their own responsibilities to the natural world.\n\nProgramming Schedule\n\n9:30 a.m. Ohèn:ton Karihwatéhkwen | Haudenosaunee Thanksgiving Address\n9:30–10:15 a.m. Turtle Meet & Greet | Keepers of the Land\n10:30 a.m. Otter | Guardians\n11:30 a.m. Polar Bear | Healers and Lessons\n12:00 p.m. Indigenous Environmental Stewardship: Historical and Ongoing\n1:30 p.m. Hellbender | Conservation in the Ohi:yo’\n2:30 p.m. Eagle | Protectors\n3:30 p.m. Sturgeon | Wisdom and Resilience\nThroughout the day, guests can also visit the Nature Cart to learn about Haudenosaunee relationships with more-than-human relatives and connect with community organizations participating in the event.\n\nThe Future Stewards Program will host a community table at the Zoo and share information about FSP, Indigenous student support at RIT, and our work with students and community partners.\n\nFSP will pay admission for RIT Indigenous students who would like to attend. Students interested in joining us should contact Kendall Scott in advance so admission can be arranged.\n\nCome spend the day learning from Haudenosaunee perspectives on culture, wildlife, conservation, and our relationships with the land and the beings we share it with.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2332433
END:VEVENT
