UID:0a97191f8aa82267595ad7e0e0ecf2d07232026_11:02:11_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Faith & Feelings: Exploring the Intersection of Spirituality and Mental Health
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2331279
DESCRIPTION:Join Spirituality and Religious Life (SRL) and Counseling and Psychological Services (CaPS) for a four-week discussion group on religion/secular worldviews/spirituality and mental health.  \n\nUnsure of what to expect?  Each week’s session will build upon the next—teaching Cognitive Behavioral Therapy and Clinical Pastoral Education tools, while helping students grow in their conception of faith or no faith—we’ll explore how Spirituality and Mental Health intersect on our life’s journey to discover and make meaning.\n\nStudents must attend all four sessions.\n\n*Originally Created by and Sponsored by Hadassah Margolis, MSW, LICSW, and the Chaplaincy Innovation Lab.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2331279
END:VEVENT
