UID:fe905ccd0241d076d9c99002c9be55878262026_11:55:28_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:River Cruise: Biodiversity of the Genesee River in One Cubic Foot
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2335415
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special river cruise on the Genesee River in Downtown Rochester! We will hear from a leader in conversation at Seneca Park Zoo and enjoy a slice of pizza. After the river cruise, we will have connection dialogue and activities before heading back to RIT. \n\nA generous slice of cheese or pepperoni pizza is included. Additional beverages and snacks are available for purchase onboard. Due to Monroe County Health Regulations, no outside food or beverages are permitted onboard.\n\nThis talk goes into the One Cubic Foot project that the Seneca Park Zoo has conducted twice on the river. The idea is that we monitor, collect, and document everything that uses the small, one cubic foot of space over the course of a normal day and night. The plants and animals are photographed by Nat Geo photographer David Liittschwager, and DNA barcodes are done of everything collected. Through this project we can talk about the health of the river through the plants and animals we find.\n\nThis event is hosted by Rochester by Water, a nonprofit organization. To learn more, visit https://rochesterbywater.org/public_cruises/speaker-slice-and-sail-cruise-aboard-riverie/.\n \nAccessibility Notes: \nRiverie is a no-step entry vessel. The boat is boarded using a ramp, accommodating wheelchairs, scooters, and walkers.\n\nAn ASL interpreter can be requested at least a week in advance. Please email E (edtpro@rit.edu) no later than 9/16 if you would like to request an ASL interpreter for this event.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2335415
END:VEVENT
