UID:65f272eab464e9cf5c213ba602098f938202026_4:11:48_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Nuestra Fuerza: Finding Mentorship and Community in STEM
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2332758
DESCRIPTION:How do you navigate a major or industry when you don’t see many people who look like you? Join MOSAIC Center and the Society for Hispanic Professional Engineers for a panel discussion featuring RIT Latino faculty, staff, and students as they share their personal journeys through STEM. Panelists will discuss the realities of representation, practical strategies for finding and becoming a mentor, and how leaning into cultural identity and community serves as a vital source of strength and resilience. Whether you are seeking advice, connection, or simply better understanding, join us as part of Hispanic/Latine Heritage Month. Time will be allotted for audience Q&A and brief networking.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2332758
END:VEVENT
