UID:cdb45cd41701e7706e103136b4d068366252026_2:42:12_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Alternative Break: Info Session
LOCATION:Bamboo Room (Campus Center 2650), 35 Lomb Memorial Dr., Rochester, NY 14623, United States
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2330443
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in applying for on of our 2027 Alternative Break Immersion Trips?\n\nThe Alternative Break (AB) program gives students the opportunity to engage with and contribute to communities around the world. Students who participate spend 5-9 days learning about critical challenges facing communities, interacting with local leaders, and performing short-term projects with community agencies.\n\nLed by the CLCE's awesome AB team, our AB Information Sessions cover all the questions you may have about our program. Information sessions are optional for anyone interested in submitting an application for our 2027 trips, but are highly encouraged for anyone who is new to the program\n\nIf you cannot make any of our Information Sessions and would like more information, please email Victoria Cirillo (vrcrli@rit.edu) to set up an individual meeting.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2330443
END:VEVENT
