UID:68fe12120045b1678bd46d764d001ff18262026_10:00:05_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:The Injured Body: A Film About Racism in America - Screening and Director Q&A 
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2335406
DESCRIPTION:The Injured Body is a film about racism, resilience, and radical imagination. It asks the question: how do we carry the weight of racism in our bodies, what does it mean for our mental and physical health, and how can we begin to heal?\n\n\nShot in Rochester and across the changing seasons of Upstate New York, the documentary delves into the everyday realities of racial microaggressions through candid conversations with 16 women of color and features mesmerizing dance sequences primarily choreographed by Mariko Yamada and portrait photography by Erica Jae. \n\n\nFollowing the screening, there will be a panel discussion with director Mara Ahmed, an RIT alum, on the complex intersections of race, gender, and identity in today’s America. All are welcome.\n---\nEvent Details: https://campusgroups.rit.edu/rsvp?id=2335406
END:VEVENT
